# Android rules

- Prefer Kotlin, coroutines/Flow with bounded buffering, and immutable domain values.
- Keep Android APIs in adapters. The navigation core must run in JVM/native tests and replay without Android services.
- Use `SensorEvent.timestamp` and the monotonic clock relationship. Do not use callback arrival wall time for fusion.
- Sensor callbacks only enqueue/copy samples. No model inference, map query, disk write, or UI work in the callback.
- Declare phone frame, vehicle frame x-forward/y-left/z-up, ENU, and WGS84 conversions in code and tests.
- Capture sensor accuracy, gaps, uncalibrated bias fields, saturation, and availability.
- Request only foreground precise location unless a documented product feature requires more.
- The core works in airplane mode after a bounded area package is installed.
- Use MapLibre Native local PMTiles for rendering and a separate compact graph for topology.
- Never download offline tiles from the public OpenStreetMap tile server.
- UI consumes `NavigationState`; visual interpolation must not modify logged estimator outputs.
- Show `LOW_CONFIDENCE` when thresholds are exceeded. Do not present lane-level precision without evidence.
- Benchmark CPU/XNNPACK before NNAPI and test each device path.
- Keep app secrets, raw datasets, private routes, and model binaries out of Git.

